  "upi unified payments interface npci psp payer psp payee psp remitter bank beneficiary bank vpa upi id collect request intent rrn deemed pending timeout reversal",
  "UPI moves money between bank accounts in seconds through NPCI's switch, with apps, banks and NPCI each playing a part. Its data comes from every step of that flow.",
  "A payer uses a UPI app run by a payment service provider (PSP), identifying the payee by a UPI ID (VPA), QR code or intent link. The payer PSP sends the request to the NPCI UPI switch, which resolves the payee's bank, asks the remitter bank to debit the payer after PIN verification, and asks the beneficiary bank to credit the payee. Each transaction gets a unique reference such as the RRN. Outcomes are success, failure, or deemed or pending when a response times out; pending transactions are resolved later through status checks, and failed debits must be reversed. Collect requests pull money, pay requests push it. Data teams track status changes, response codes and timings at each hop.",
