  "refunds chargebacks disputes reason codes representment arbitration merchant initiated refund customer complaint tat turnaround time upi dispute card network",
  "Refunds are returns started by the merchant, while chargebacks and disputes are started by the customer through their bank, with deadlines, evidence and rules set by the networks.",
  "A refund is initiated by the merchant, fully or partially, and linked to the original transaction, with its own status and timings. A dispute or chargeback starts when a customer complains to their bank, for example \"amount debited but not credited\" or \"goods not received\". The bank raises it through the network with a reason code; the merchant or acquirer can accept it or contest it with evidence (representment), and unresolved cases can go to arbitration. Each step has a turnaround time, and RBI's harmonised turnaround time rules require compensation when failed transactions aren't reversed in time. Data teams track dispute rates, reasons, win rates, ageing and the cost of losses.",
